        "type": "utterance",
        "payload": {
          "text": "Build a small Python CLI package called `unitconvert` in the current repository. Work step by step, and briefly state what you are about to do before each action.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Create a package directory `unitconvert/` with an `__init__.py`.\n2. `unitconvert/temperature.py` — functions with type hints: `celsius_to_fahrenheit`, `fahrenheit_to_celsius`, `celsius_to_kelvin`, `kelvin_to_celsius`.\n3. `unitconvert/length.py` — functions with type hints: `meters_to_feet`, `feet_to_meters`, `km_to_miles`, `miles_to_km`.\n4. `unitconvert/cli.py` — an argparse-based CLI invoked as `python -m unitconvert <category> <from_unit> <to_unit> <value>` that prints the converted numeric result. Support categories `temperature` and `length`.\n5. `tests/test_temperature.py` and `tests/test_length.py` — pytest tests covering each function plus at least one edge case each (e.g. 0 degrees, round-trip conversion).\n6. Run the suite with `python -m pytest -q` and fix any failures until everything passes.\n7. Update `README.md` with installation and usage examples for the CLI.\n\nConstraints: keep functions small and single-purpose, use clear names, and do not add third-party dependencies (standard library + pytest only)."
        }
